# What EAS Build uploads from this repository: EAS archives the git repo from its root, and with
# this file there it reads no .gitignore, so this is the whole list. The iOS app needs only
# mobile/, without what is generated or installed there; .git stays, as it does without this file.
# No trailing slashes: eas-cli asks about directories by bare path ("mobile"), which a pattern
# like "!/mobile/" never matches. mobile/check.ts checks this list with eas-cli's own copy.
/*
!/.git
!/mobile
/mobile/node_modules
/mobile/.expo
/mobile/ios
/mobile/android
/mobile/*.tsbuildinfo
